[38;5;231m⏺[39m That answer has a tell in it worth surfacing: watching only makes sense if changes arrive from somewhere you're not
  looking. If you're the only one editing tasks, you already know when one changed — you changed it. So a "watch"
  feature implies some other source of change.

  Which means the multi-user question from before isn't really unresolved; it's hiding inside this one:

